{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Bullish Momentum: The model consistently fails to capture the magnitude of upward price spikes (e.g., the surge from ~76 to ~89 in late November), forecasting near-linear trends while true outcomes exhibit exponential jumps. Apply a positive bias adjustment when recent history shows a sustained upward trajectory, regardless of low sentiment scores.",
    "Sentiment Lag Correction: The model ignores sentiment signals (0.20-0.50) that precede price rallies. When sentiment history contains values > 0.20, immediately increase the forecast slope to anticipate a breakout rather than maintaining a flat or slightly rising baseline.",
    "Failure to Anticipate Mean Reversion: The model projects continued gradual increases even after the price peak (~89), failing to account for the subsequent sharp correction and volatility. Implement a mean-reversion heuristic that reduces the forecast slope or introduces a downward correction once prices exceed the 90th percentile of the recent 30-day history.",
    "Horizon-Specific Overshoot: The model's error grows significantly with the forecast horizon (30-day view), suggesting it treats short-term noise as long-term trend. Reduce the forecasted growth rate for horizons beyond 10 days to prevent overestimation of the peak and underestimation of the subsequent decline."
  ]
}
